          "text": "**Track:** styles | **Difficulty:** 5/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "19th-century Romanticism stretches forms for emotional narrative — bigger orchestras, chromatic harmony, virtuoso solo writing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "harmony",
      "title": "Harmony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Borrowed chords, augmented sixths, extended dominants colour mood. Nationalist composers (Dvořák, Grieg, Sibelius) embed folk dances in symphonic works."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "in-trad",
      "title": "In trad",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Lush piano intros to airs, dramatic key changes in céilí sets, vibrato-heavy string treatment. Use Romantic tools where story needs shadow — not every reel wants a Rachmaninoff ending."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
